+# Bug Assessment: Product deletion breaks carts and historical orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Deleting a product through `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}` must not break carts or orders. Existing cart lines for the deleted product must disappear while the cart remains usable and recalculated; adding the deleted SKU must return 404. Historical order lines must remain readable with their purchased snapshot values and unchanged totals across merchant/customer endpoints, and order status changes and checkout must continue to work. The deleted product must also be unavailable through `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` without affecting other products.
+
+## Symptom
+
+The cart persistence stores product identity as product ID/SKU but repopulation resolves the current product and marks missing products obsolete. The cart read path then deletes/returns no cart, while the data populator dereferences `item.getProduct()`. Order product rows already contain SKU, name, quantity and charge, but both order presentation paths attempt a live product lookup for optional enrichment; deletion therefore risks incomplete or failing order responses.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a product, add it to a cart, and create an order containing it.
+2. Delete the product with `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}`.
+3. Read the cart and order through the listed merchant/customer endpoints; also try cart updates, checkout, adding the deleted SKU, and `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}`.
+
+The report does not specify a fixture, authentication setup, or exact response JSON shape: [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: integration environment and fixture details].
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/ProductServiceImpl.java:214-245` — hard-deletes the product and its dependent catalog data.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java:184-204` — `getByCode` deletes/returns a cart when repopulation marks it obsolete.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java:230-359` — resolves each cart item by SKU, marks missing products obsolete, and otherwise calculates live pricing.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java:96-202` — assumes every cart item has a live product and calculates the response from repopulated items.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java:189-267` — rejects missing SKUs when adding cart items, with the SKU form already mapped to `ResourceNotFoundException`.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java:59-133` and `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java:63-114` — correctly copy stored order fields but use a live product lookup for optional product/image enrichment.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductFacadeV2Impl.java:89-111` — translates a missing SKU lookup to `ResourceNotFoundException`, which should yield 404.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/orderproduct/OrderProduct.java:25-58` — stores historical SKU, name, quantity and one-time charge independently of the catalog product.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. Product deletion removes the live catalog row, while cart loading treats a missing live product as an obsolete cart rather than removing only that line, and cart/order presentation code is not consistently defensive about the missing association. Historical order data is already modeled as a snapshot, so the preferred fix is to preserve that snapshot behavior and make deleted-product handling explicit at cart repopulation and order enrichment boundaries.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: When a persisted cart item cannot resolve its SKU, remove that item and its cart attributes from the cart, but keep the cart itself, recalculate totals/quantity from remaining live items, and allow an empty cart to be returned and updated. Ensure all add-to-cart paths retain the existing not-found exception mapping for a missing SKU. Make order product conversion rely on the stored `OrderProduct` fields and treat live product lookup as optional enrichment, so deleted products do not affect order lines or totals. Keep the v2 SKU lookup's missing-product exception as HTTP 404.
+
+Update the product deletion/cart/order integration or service tests to cover mixed and product-only carts, cart mutation and checkout, deleted SKU insertion, all order read endpoints and status update, v2 404, and preservation of another product.
+
+**Alternatives** (optional):
+- Soft-delete products and retain all associations, but this changes deletion semantics and requires filtering soft-deleted products throughout catalog queries.
+- Copy product data into cart rows as well as order rows, but this increases schema/migration scope and is unnecessary if deleted cart lines are removed.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/ReadableOrderProductPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/cart/ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest.java`
+- relevant order/product integration test files under `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Verify deletion removes only deleted lines from a cart, preserves an empty cart, recalculates quantity/subtotal/total, and permits update/multi-update/checkout.
+- Verify adding a deleted SKU returns 404 and v2 lookup returns 404.
+- Verify merchant and customer order reads and lists retain stored SKU/name/quantity/price/subtotal/totals, and status update still succeeds after deletion.
+- Verify another product is unchanged.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Cart cleanup must remove child attribute rows safely and avoid deleting the cart or causing lazy-loading failures.
+- Checkout must not receive deleted items or attempt to charge them; empty-cart checkout behavior should remain the platform's existing behavior.
+- Order output must not substitute current catalog price/name for stored historical values.
+- Existing API exception translation and unrelated-product behavior must remain unchanged.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact integration fixture/authentication and checkout payment setup are not included in the ticket.]
