+# Bug Fix: Product deletion breaks carts and historical orders
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T22:45:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Cart loading now removes only persisted lines whose SKU no longer resolves, including their child attributes, and preserves the cart for recalculation and later updates. The cart response explicitly exposes an empty product list, and its populator tolerates any remaining detached line; add-to-cart and v2 missing-SKU handling already provide the required 404 behavior, while order converters already use stored order-product snapshots and only enrich from a live product when available.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` | modified | Remove obsolete product lines and attributes instead of marking/deleting the entire cart; retain and update the cart. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartDataPopulator.java` | modified | Skip detached lines defensively and always set the response product list, including empty carts. |
+
+## Diff Highlights
+
+Missing products are collected while iterating over a copy of the line-item set, then their attributes and item rows are deleted and the surviving set is saved. The cart is no longer marked obsolete merely because it has no lines, so totals can be calculated as zero and the cart remains addressable.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No new automated fixture was added: the repository's existing API tests require a larger authenticated integration fixture, and the ticket did not provide checkout/payment setup. The changed modules were compiled and the existing cart test was selected for the verification stage.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed; all six reactor modules compiled successfully.
+- Manual checks: inspected the existing add-to-cart missing-SKU and v2 missing-product exception paths, plus order snapshot fields and converters.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The order populator/mapper did not require a code change: both already copy SKU, name, quantity, and stored charge before treating the live product lookup as optional enrichment. No source changes outside the cart service and cart response populator were necessary.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add an authenticated end-to-end regression fixture covering deletion, cart mutation/checkout, all order endpoints, and status updates when the integration test environment is available.
